Heinkel: [Miss Filóre, about what you said earlier…]

Filóre: [Ah, that was some splendid tact! Rest assured. I also made sure to tell the envoy to inform the people at the treatment center that it was your idea, Heinkel-sama.]

Heinkel: [――. You need to have more self-restraint. And frankly, more self-respect too.]

Filóre: [Self-restraint!? I don’t like those words…!]

As if betrayed by her cheerful smile, Filóre turned pale as she staggered towards a bench within the chapel. While watching over her state, he let a deep exhale out of his nose.

