Heinkel: [But, because they heard it was my suggestion, the earlier matter with the treatment center might not go over so well. The fact that it wouldn’t be strange for such a thing to happen is the epitome of my current standing. Sorry, but I’m aware of it.]

Filóre: [――Hk.]

His answer appeared to frustrate Filóre, but since it was none other than himself who had caused her to make that face, Heinkel did not possess the words to comfort or encourage her.

To be perfectly honest, he was still regretting his decision. ――As expected, Heinkel should not have accepted the request of Filóre, which could only be seen as delusional.

Whenever he witnessed the attitude of his master, a girl who, while still clumsy, was earnestly taking part in the Royal Selection, more and more did he end up despising his own self, who served as naught but a hindrance to her ambitions.

Doubly so if when considering that all the infamy he had accrued until now had been earned through his own volition.

Heinkel: [In the end, nothing I do ever goes well…]

