Heinkel: […If Miss Filóre becomes the Monarch, huh? So, does that mean whenever you help others at the Church, it’s just a calculated act?]

Filóre: [Could you please not say such outrageous things!? You see, this is all an extremely good deal. By giving counsel to the people who come to the Church, they get help with their troubles, and I also build a reputation for doing good things, and it also feels nice for us when we do a good thing… right?]

Heinkel: [Don’t lump me in there as if it’s only natural. I’m…]

Filóre: [But, don’t you think it’s joyous to receive gratitude from others? That’s how it is for me. That’s why, even if the title of Saintess is heavy to shoulder, I quite like the Church.]

Puffing her chest out with a nod, Filóre’s words rendered Heinkel unable to respond.

