――Within the current Kingdom of Lugunica, the role fulfilled by the Church of the Divine Dragon was a major one.

To begin with, the Kingdom of Lugunica was under the protection of the Divine Dragon Volcanica, and with such stability and protection of the nation promised to them, they had continued to thrive until today.

That alone was enough to naturally fill the majority of the Kingdom’s citizens with feelings of reverence towards the Divine Dragon, so inevitably, it also led to their unconditional faith in the Church of the Divine Dragon.

Heinkel was no exception to that, and that was precisely why when his wife fell into a slumber from which she never awoke, he began making frequent visits to the church, placing his belief in the house of prayer and miracle.

Regrettably, Heinkel’s prayers had borne no fruit, and he had gone on to commit a momentous transgression such that he could no longer bring himself to face the Divine Dragon or its followers. Since then, he had grown distant from the Church, hence why he could not help but scoff at how ill-suited his current position was.

But once he finished deploring that foolishness of his, Heinkel had no choice but to confront it directly. The distrust towards the Church of the Divine Dragon burgeoning within himself―― regarding the existence of Filóre. To be precise, regarding the Church’s intentions in having Filóre participate in the Royal Selection.

Appointed as her Knight, what had become painfully clear to him from observing Filóre at such a close proximity, was that she possessed an innate goodness with no ulterior motives whatsoever, to the point it was somewhat frightening.

In absolutely everything, no matter who stood before her, Filóre would always give her all, and ignoring her concerning sense of judgment when it came to naming Heinkel as her Knight, whenever she was pressed for a decision, rather than panicking, she made her choice on her own responsibility, possessing the ability to take action in order to bring those decisions to fruition.

